schema ExternalEstateDescriptor
generation external-estate-1
authority ForeignTwin + ProviderGraph + CapabilityClosure

field domain
  type set[text]
  role reusable-world-context

field estate_role
  type set[material_source, media_service, action_adapter, interaction_reference, design_reference, authoring_adapter, compiler_toolchain, transport_carrier, publication_carrier, verification_tool, external_service_candidate, reference_standard]
  role compositional-reagent-class

field topic_domain
  type set[text]
  role direct-human-material-match

field semantic_output
  type set[text]
  role typed-foreign-observation

field affordance
  type set[text]
  role reusable-capability-class

field carrier
  type enum[http,feed,mcp,a2a,x402,protocol,file,unknown]
  role physical-access-carrier

field truth_level
  type enum[observed_candidate]
  role source-standing

invariant heterogeneous-density
  statement broad reuse may name many unrelated possible contexts, but a human World result requires direct topic evidence and an appropriate estate role; a carrier or toolchain label alone is not material

invariant semantic-owner-separation
  statement an external descriptor contributes candidate observations and realization options only; Identity, Authority, Evidence, Money and Work remain independently owned

forbidden_inference listed source -> live endpoint
forbidden_inference public descriptor -> credential or remote account binding
forbidden_inference capability advertisement -> authority, payment approval, provider admission or effect right
forbidden_inference one domain label -> the complete set of worlds that can use an observation
forbidden_inference broad reuse or carrier default -> direct human material for that domain
